00:09:22.470 --> 00:09:26.928
So Hannah, as a navy veteran,
did you drove heavily on your

00:09:26.928 --> 00:09:31.834
military experience in your
application as says and are there any

00:09:31.834 --> 00:09:37.473
recommendations generally that you
want to give on applying the veteran?

00:09:37.473 --> 00:09:40.908
&gt;&gt; Definitely, so I think reach out
to the veterans club we love talking

00:09:40.908 --> 00:09:43.169
to applicants but
in terms of talking about.

00:09:43.169 --> 00:09:44.732
&gt;&gt; How can they reach
out to veterans club?

00:09:44.732 --> 00:09:48.521
&gt;&gt; We have a GSP veterans club page in
those like a little box you can fill

00:09:48.521 --> 00:09:53.180
out there and we'll get your email and
someone from the club will respond.

00:09:53.180 --> 00:09:57.020
But in terms of the application, I think
the best piece of advice that I got was

00:09:57.020 --> 00:10:00.100
that it should be
uncomfortable writing it and

00:10:00.100 --> 00:10:03.250
it should really kind of dig
to the core of who you are.

00:10:03.250 --> 00:10:06.770
And for me that did include
a deployment story from the military.

00:10:06.770 --> 00:10:07.900
I do not think it has to though.

00:10:07.900 --> 00:10:09.180
I just think it has to be.

00:10:09.180 --> 00:10:12.380
Something personal that really gets
to the core of who you are and for

00:10:12.380 --> 00:10:16.050
a lot of veterans that is something
about their military experience.

00:10:16.050 --> 00:10:19.720
because the rest of your application is
talking about all of your accomplishments.

00:10:19.720 --> 00:10:23.840
Where the essay is the one part to really
hone in as to who you are as a person.

00:10:23.840 --> 00:10:24.516
&gt;&gt; Amazing.

00:10:24.516 --> 00:10:27.630
Thanks for sharing that.

00:10:27.630 --> 00:10:32.811
So this next one, I'll take it first,
what surprised you most at the GSP?

00:10:34.170 --> 00:10:36.610
I think as an international student,

00:10:36.610 --> 00:10:40.310
there has been a lot of like
surprises to me, not only me.

00:10:40.310 --> 00:10:42.830
But just like, you know,
moving from my country and

00:10:42.830 --> 00:10:47.350
calling total different culture and
experiences and all of that.

00:10:47.350 --> 00:10:50.630
But I think the thing that I
was pleasantly surprised at

00:10:50.630 --> 00:10:52.960
the GSP is my classmates.

00:10:52.960 --> 00:10:57.690
Just how diverse they are,
how slick amazing and

00:10:57.690 --> 00:11:01.500
smart and ambitious and
driven people are around me.

00:11:01.500 --> 00:11:06.460
I think that was one of the things
that surprised me most at the GSP is

00:11:06.460 --> 00:11:09.990
that I thought that I managed
to create home away from home.

00:11:09.990 --> 00:11:15.670
And just piece it out with people that you
can literally learn from every hour like,

00:11:15.670 --> 00:11:16.220
basically.

00:11:17.230 --> 00:11:18.790
What's surprised you most at the GSP,
Hannah?

00:11:18.790 --> 00:11:21.240
&gt;&gt; I think it's specially second year.

00:11:21.240 --> 00:11:24.750
A lot of times it kind of
feels like an all day podcast,

00:11:24.750 --> 00:11:27.400
where you're just constantly listening and
learning.

00:11:27.400 --> 00:11:30.620
And getting your perspective challenged,
kind of growing mentally.

00:11:30.620 --> 00:11:34.460
And I think when you're working, you're
used to just showing up at certain time

00:11:34.460 --> 00:11:37.060
kind of grinding and
then ending at a certain time.

00:11:37.060 --> 00:11:39.980
Whereas an MBA student you just
really get to step back and really

00:11:39.980 --> 00:11:43.840
have your perspective, challenge learn
about who's really interesting things.

00:11:43.840 --> 00:11:45.139
And that's been surprising.

00:11:46.500 --> 00:11:48.130
&gt;&gt; Yeah, amazing.

00:11:48.130 --> 00:11:52.465
Well, I just want to remind everyone that
